        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0833" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.5/5–1554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-15T10:00:00+01:00">May 15, 1954—10 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dulte 70. Limit distribution. I took occasion to tell Bidault last night that we
                    should be under no illusions about troop withdrawal in Indochina, that it would
                    be very difficult to prevent any lines fixed from developing into <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> partition which was something US could not
                    accept. If we saw things heading that way, we would have to disassociate
                    ourselves from this particular proposal.</p>
                <p>Bidault replied that would be very serious. He said that military regrouping
                    would postpone any political settlement and that neither Vietnamese nor Viet
                    Minh would accept partition. He realized that if there were any clean-cut split
                    on a given parallel, it would inevitably become partition and for that reason he
                    felt jumbled and irregular lines like frontiers of Israel far safer. I said I
                    agreed with this line of thought.</p>
                <p>I also told him that we were making progress with British and I felt much more
                    optimistic than two weeks ago. I also said we could do a great deal for the long
                    pull, including training, provided it was not necessary for us to intervene
                    directly in present fighting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
